@endpoint("/admin-api/risk",
  "get",
  #{
    `operationId`:"getRisk",
    `summary`:"The risk datasets, a lookup, and the refused passwords",
    `description`:"Which `store` holds the risk data (the database, or this process where there is none); every dataset in `datasets` with its `state` (active, stale or empty), active and previous version, publication date, row count, provider attribution and every recorded `versions` row (refused ones with their `refusal`); the `formats` a file may be in; with `address`, what the active datasets say about it in `lookup` (`geo`, `asn`, `lists`, the `datasets` versions that answered and any `stale` ones left out); with `authenticator`, what the active FIDO MDS3 BLOB says about that key in `authenticatorLookup` (`keyKind`, `key`, `listed`, `why` when it is not, `version`, `stale`, and the listed `model`: `description`, `protocolFamily`, `certificationLevel`, `latestStatus`, `compromised`, `statusReports`, `metadataStatement`); and a page of the realm's refused passwords in `failures` — a subject or a name's digest, the door, the network prefix, the ASN and the code, never an address. A page of the realm's assessed sign-ins in `assessments` (`{ total, rows }`, the last 7 days, newest first; each row's first signal is the model's, with its `factors`, the user term's `terms`, and `unknown`, the levels whose lookup found nothing — `asn`, `country`, `browser`, `os`, `device` — which the model counts as unseen) and of its people by current standing in `subjects`, each with its `assessmentsPaging` / `subjectsPaging`. Every row naming a person's `subject` also carries their `username` ('' when the directory no longer holds them).\n\n**Mirrors** `GET /admin/risk` on the admin console.",
    `tags`:#["Risk"],
    `responses`:#{
      `200`:#{
        `description`:"The datasets, the lookup, the failures, the assessments and the standings.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `default`:#{
        `description`:"A refusal or a failure.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      }
    },
    `parameters`:#[
      #{
        `name`:"address",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"An IPv4 or IPv6 address to look up."
      },
      #{
        `name`:"authenticator",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"An AAGUID, an AAID (`XXXX#XXXX`) or an attestation certificate key identifier (40 hex digits) to look up in the FIDO metadata (#1080)."
      },
      #{
        `name`:"level",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"Only the assessments at this level."
      },
      #{
        `name`:"subject",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"Only this person's assessments."
      },
      #{
        `name`:"per",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"Rows per page. Defaults to 50 and is capped at 300. On a drill-down it is SHARED by every list in the reply, which each carry a page number of their own."
      },
      #{
        `name`:"assessmentsPage",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"Which page of `assessments` to return, answered by `assessmentsPaging`. The sign-ins assessed in the last 7 days, newest first, 50 by default."
      },
      #{
        `name`:"subjectsPage",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"Which page of `subjects` to return, answered by `subjectsPaging`. The realm's people by current standing, highest score first, twenty-five by default."
      },
      #{
        `name`:"failuresPage",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"Which page of `failures` to return, answered by `failuresPaging`. The refused passwords of the last 7 days, newest first, fifty by default (#313)."
      }
    ],
    `security`:#[#{`oauth2`:#["admin:read"]},#{`bearerAuth`:#[]}]
  })
