    `description`:"THIS NODE only — the front process that answers and its own request and hosted-surface worker THREADS, never another node of a cluster. `target` is `all` (the default: the front process's main thread and every ready worker thread), `front`, or a worker thread's `threadId` as GET /admin-api/node-health lists it. Each worker thread is a V8 isolate of its own and collects itself, asked over the pool's channel and waited for up to ten seconds. A FULL COLLECTION STOPS THE THREAD IT RUNS IN UNTIL IT FINISHES; in the front process that pauses every listener of the node. A diagnostic. Answers 200 with `rows`, one per isolate collected or asked (`kind` `process` or `thread`, `pid`, `threadId`, `role`, `ok`, `heapUsedBeforeBytes`, `heapTotalBeforeBytes`, `heapUsedAfterBytes`, `heapTotalAfterBytes`, `freedBytes`, `durationMs` — the pause — and `error`), `unanswered` (worker threads that did not answer in time), `totals` and `message`; 400 for an unknown action or a malformed `target`, 404 for a thread this node does not have, 500 when the front process alone was asked and could not collect. Audited. A service operation: a realm's own administrator is refused it.\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/node-health` on the admin console.",
