@endpoint("/admin-api/users/add-certificate",
  "post",
  #{
    `operationId`:"addUserCertificate",
    `summary`:"Store a certificate on somebody's entry, so an outside certificate authority's certificate signs them in",
    `description`:"Stores one X.509 certificate in the person's `userCertificate` (RFC 4523; written as `userCertificate;binary`). A certificate from an outside certificate authority — one trusted through the Client Truststores — is an identity at a door that reads a client certificate as a person (/tls/sign-in, the sign-in screen, SCIM, the XACML gates, Shared Signals, WS-Trust, LDAP SASL EXTERNAL) only while it is stored, byte for byte, on exactly one entry of the realm: never by its common name or subject (#1061). Refused when it is already stored on another entry (STS-ADMIN-0899) or the person has no entry (STS-ADMIN-0898). A renewed certificate is stored again.\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/users, POST /admin/users/new, POST /admin/users/edit and POST /admin/users/service-account` on the admin console.",
    `tags`:#["Users"],
    `responses`:#{
      `200`:#{
        `description`:"The certificates the entry stores now.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `400`:#{
        `description`:"The operation was refused; `errors` says why and nothing changed.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `default`:#{
        `description`:"A refusal or a failure.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      }
    },
    `requestBody`:#{`required`:true,`content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}},
    `security`:#[#{`oauth2`:#["admin:write"]},#{`bearerAuth`:#[]}]
  })
op `addUserCertificate`(@js(#{
    `examples`:#[
      #{
        `user`:"alice",
