@endpoint("/admin-api/users/enrol-self-issued-subject",
  "post",
  #{
    `operationId`:"enrolUserSelfIssuedSubject",
    `summary`:"Enrol a self-issued (SIOPv2) subject for somebody",
    `description`:"Enrols a did:jwk, did:key or did:web, an RFC 9278 JWK thumbprint URI, a base64url SHA-256 JWK thumbprint or a public JWK (as JSON) on the person's entry. A self-issued ID Token signed by that key then signs them in, while oid4vp.signInSelfIssued is on. Refused where the subject is already enrolled for anybody in the realm. A person enrols their own on /portal/self-issued by proving the key with their wallet.\n\nWhat this enrols is recorded as BY VALUE (`proof: admin`, unproven), and nothing that releases or binds a subject reads it. A did:web's DID document is fetched now and every authentication key it names is pinned; a later sign-in with any other key is refused (STS-VC-0126). A document that cannot be fetched or names no such key is refused (STS-ADMIN-0871) (#693).\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/users, POST /admin/users/new, POST /admin/users/edit and POST /admin/users/service-account` on the admin console.",
    `tags`:#["Users"],
    `responses`:#{
      `200`:#{
        `description`:"The subject as enrolled.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `400`:#{
        `description`:"The operation was refused; `errors` says why and nothing changed.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `default`:#{
        `description`:"A refusal or a failure.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      }
    },
    `requestBody`:#{`required`:true,`content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}},
    `security`:#[#{`oauth2`:#["admin:write"]},#{`bearerAuth`:#[]}]
  })
op `enrolUserSelfIssuedSubject`(@js(#{
    `examples`:#[
      #{
        `user`:"alice",
        `subject`:"did:jwk:eyJrdHkiOiJPS1AiLCJjcnYiOiJFZDI1NTE5IiwieCI6IjEyMyJ9",
        `label`:"phone wallet"
      }
    ]
  }) `requestBody/content/application~1json/schema`: {
