@endpoint("/admin-api/users/deactivate-published-did",
  "post",
  #{
    `operationId`:"deactivateUserPublishedDid",
    `summary`:"Deactivate a did:web this realm publishes for somebody",
    `description`:"Deactivates one of the person's published DIDs (#1291): its address answers 410 Gone with `{ id, deactivated: true }` for good, a resolver reports `deactivated: true`, its version history stays resolvable, and it no longer signs the person in, nor is it preferred or released in the `did` claim. A deactivated DID is never reactivated. An administrator never creates or changes one: that is the person's act on /portal/self-issued. A DID the person does not hold, or one already deactivated, is refused (STS-VC-0172).\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/users, POST /admin/users/new, POST /admin/users/edit and POST /admin/users/service-account` on the admin console.",
