  #{
    `operationId`:"clearSecurityKey",
    `summary`:"Remove one of somebody's security keys",
    `description`:"Goes through the same `removeKey()` the person's own portal calls, which is what carries the refusal that matters: **it will not remove the last way in.** A person with no password whose only PRIMARY key this is would be locked out by an operator's call, and an operator must not be able to do what the owner is stopped from doing.\n\nThe credential id is the base64url one on `GET /admin-api/mfa`'s rows and on `/portal/keys`.\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/users` on the admin console.",
