  `responses/200/content/application~1json/schema`: `SharedModel179`,
  `responses/400/content/application~1json/schema`: `SharedModel179`,
  `responses/default/content/application~1json/schema`: `SharedModel1`): void;
  

@endpoint("/admin-api/realms/update",
  "post",
  #{
    `operationId`:"updateRealm",
    `summary`:"Rename a realm, or describe it",
    `description`:"The `id` cannot be changed, because it is the path segment every client was given. Define a new realm and remove this one if that is what is wanted — and note that the new one gets a new signing key, which is the honest consequence of it being a different realm. The `domain` is fixed for the same kind of reason: a `domain` other than the realm's own is refused (STS-CORE-0101), and the same value again is accepted and changes nothing.\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/realms` on the admin console.",
