@endpoint("/admin-api/realms/set",
  "post",
  #{
    `operationId`:"setRealmSetting",
    `summary`:"Set one setting on one realm",
    `description`:"The value applies to the next request that arrives under that realm's prefix and to nothing else — above whatever the process as a whole is configured with, and below nothing.\n\nThis is the same store `POST /realm/<id>/admin-api/config/set` writes to, and either is fine; the difference is only which realm you have to be in to make the call. A setting whose `editable` is false is refused with the reason, exactly as it is on the service-wide resource, and every `realms.*` key is refused outright. `realms.maxCount` is process-wide; only the default realm's service administrator changes it, and a create past that limit is refused. Lowering the limit does not remove realms.\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/realms` on the admin console.",
