@endpoint("/admin-api/totp",
  "get",
  #{
    `operationId`:"getTotpSettings",
    `summary`:"The authenticator-app second factor's settings",
    `description`:"The eight `totp.*` settings — the HMAC digest, the digits, the seconds in a step, the steps of clock skew forgiven, the shared secret length, the label an app shows, whether new enrolments are offered at all, and how long an unconfirmed one lives — with the RFC 6238 algorithm table in `status`, read from `common/totp.ts` rather than written down here.\n\n**CHANGING THE DIGEST, THE DIGITS OR THE PERIOD AFFECTS NEW ENROLMENTS ONLY.** An existing secret is verified with the parameters it was enrolled under — the ones the QR code told the app — because this service cannot change them retrospectively. `totp.window` is the exception and applies to everybody.\n\n**Codes are verified FOR REAL in both modes**, which almost nothing else in this service is. Who holds an enrolment is `GET /users` (or `GET /mfa`), and clearing one is `POST /users/clear-totp`.\n\nThese eight were on `GET /admin-api/mfa` until 2026-09-10, when the console page that drew them split into a mechanism page and a roster.\n\nTHERE IS NO POST BESIDE THIS ONE and that is not a gap: every form on the console page this mirrors posts `set-many` to /admin/config, so `POST /admin-api/config/set-many` is already the operation for it. One store, one action, two doors.\n\n**Mirrors** `GET /admin/totp` on the admin console.\n\nThe reply also carries `protocolEndpoints`: every endpoint of this family in the realm the call arrived in, as `{ name, methods, url }` (plus `route` for an HTTP endpoint, `transport` for a socket, and `registered: false` for a route the router no longer has).",
    `tags`:#["TOTP MFA"],
    `responses`:#{
      `200`:#{
        `description`:"What the page says, and the settings it draws — described rows carrying each value's source and whether it can be changed while the service runs.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `400`:#{
        `description`:"The answer.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `default`:#{
        `description`:"A refusal or a failure.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      }
    },
    `security`:#[#{`oauth2`:#["admin:read"]},#{`bearerAuth`:#[]}]
  })
op `getTotpSettings`(`responses/200/content/application~1json/schema`: {
    `page`?: string;
    `title`?: string;
    `what`?: string;
    `notes`?: (string)[];
    `links`?: ({`href`?: string; `what`?: string})[];
    `settings`?: `SharedModel153`;
    `leadHtml`?: string;
    `alsoHtml`?: (string)[];
