@endpoint("/admin-api/wsfed",
  "get",
  #{
    `operationId`:"getWsFedSettings",
    `summary`:"The passive requestor profile's page",
    `description`:"No setting of its own. The entity ID this service names itself by in the metadata and a sign-in response is the realm's OAuth issuer, not a setting (#523), and the assertion's lifetime is `wsfed.assertionLifetimeMin`, homed with the other assertion lifetimes on `/admin/saml2`.\n\nThe assertion it carries is a SAML 1.1 one, whose contents are `GET /saml-attributes`. A `wauth` the session cannot meet is a step-up through the sign-in screen, and `wreqptr` is never dereferenced; neither is a setting, and the page says so rather than implying a missing one.\n\nTHERE IS NO POST BESIDE THIS ONE and that is not a gap: every form on the console page this mirrors posts `set-many` to /admin/config, so `POST /admin-api/config/set-many` is already the operation for it. One store, one action, two doors.\n\n**Mirrors** `GET /admin/wsfed` on the admin console.\n\nThe reply also carries `protocolEndpoints`: every endpoint of this family in the realm the call arrived in, as `{ name, methods, url }` (plus `route` for an HTTP endpoint, `transport` for a socket, and `registered: false` for a route the router no longer has).",
