    `description`:"With `state`: what the Verifier decided, with `found: true`: `state`, `nonce`, `client_id`, `requested`, `dcql_query`, `received` (whether a wallet has answered) and `verdict` (`ok`, `checks`, `claims`, `disclosed`, …, and `presentationDigest`, the SHA-256 of the presentation, which is never kept itself; null until it answers). A state this realm holds no record of is 404 with `found: false` (STS-VC-0042).\n\nWithout `state`: the realm's open verifications, newest first — at most `limit` of `total` — each its `state`, what was asked (`format`, `responseType`, `responseMode`, `byReference`, `clientId`, `requested`), `expiresAt`, and what was decided (`received`, `ok`, `decidedAt`, the disclosed claim NAMES, `failedChecks`, a wallet's `error`). A wallet SIGN-IN is not listed: it is a person signing in, not a verification an administrator asked for. The Verifier request tab draws this list.\n\n**Mirrors** `GET /admin/vc` on the admin console.\n\nThe reply also carries `protocolEndpoints`: every endpoint of this family in the realm the call arrived in, as `{ name, methods, url }` (plus `route` for an HTTP endpoint, `transport` for a socket, and `registered: false` for a route the router no longer has).",
