@endpoint("/admin-api/federation/enable",
  "post",
  #{
    `operationId`:"enableFederationRelationship",
    `summary`:"Turn a relationship on",
    `description`:"The second, deliberate act. **It is allowed on a relationship that is not fully configured**, and that is not a gap: a half-configured partner is a state somebody is passing through, and refusing to save it would mean configuring everything in one request with no way back. What happens in that state is that every endpoint for the relationship REFUSES and says which fields are missing — it never half-works — and the reply to this operation says so too.\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/federation` on the admin console.",
    `tags`:#["Federation"],
    `responses`:#{
      `200`:#{
        `description`:"The relationship, and whether it is now usable.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
