@endpoint("/admin-api/federation/rotate-key",
  "post",
  #{
    `operationId`:"rotateFederationKey",
    `summary`:"Rotate a relationship's encryption key",
    `description`:"SAML 2.0, WS-Federation and OpenID Connect service-provider-side relationships only (#168). A new key of the relationship's `fedEncryptionKeyType` is issued under this realm's Intermediate and becomes CURRENT — what `/federation/metadata/{id}` and `/federation/jwks/{id}` publish. The key it replaces still DECRYPTS for `federation.encryptionKeyGraceS`, so a partner still holding the old certificate is not refused mid-change, and then decrypts nothing; the scheduler job `federation.encryption-key-retire` removes it. A second rotation inside that window drops the older key at once. Also the way to issue a key for a relationship that has none.\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/federation` on the admin console.",
    `tags`:#["Federation"],
    `responses`:#{
      `200`:#{
        `description`:"The new key's kid, and the relationship as it now stands.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `400`:#{
        `description`:"The operation was refused; `errors` says why and nothing changed.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `default`:#{
        `description`:"A refusal or a failure.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      }
    },
    `requestBody`:#{`required`:true,`content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}},
    `security`:#[#{`oauth2`:#["admin:write"]},#{`bearerAuth`:#[]}]
  })
