    `description`:"The console's OAuth 2.0 / OpenID Connect claims table, a column per set. Each of `access_token`, `id_token` and `userinfo` that is sent is the whole list of catalogue attributes that set should carry. A set sent with exactly the selection in force is LEFT AS IT IS — the realm's, if the application was inheriting it — and a set that differs becomes the application's own selection, replacing the realm's for it, as `set-claim-attributes` writes one. A set not sent is not touched. Every set is checked before any is written. Refused (`STS-REG-0215`) for an attribute the catalogue does not hold, or an application not declared for OAuth 2.0 or OpenID Connect.\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/applications, POST /admin/applications/new, POST /admin/applications/edit and POST /admin/applications/owners` on the admin console.",
