    `description`:"Adds to `type`'s `xacml` mapping the row for `path`, or replaces the row already mapping that path: the member of an RFC 9396 detail of the type that becomes the attribute `attributeId` when an application's fine-grained authorization policy decides it. `category` (resource by default), `dataType` (string by default) and `multiplicity` (single or bag) take AuthZEN's catalogue names or the XACML URIs. The row is read by the mapping's grammar before it is written, and refused (`STS-FGA-0023`, with `field` naming the member that was wrong) for a path that is not a member path or names `type` or a common data field, an identifier this service reserves for what it writes itself (`urn:sts:xacml:*`, subject-id, resource-id, action-id, the current-time attributes, or a bare directory name in a subject category), or a category, data type or multiplicity outside the set. On an application that enforces fine-grained authorization the write is also held to coverage (`STS-FGA-0019`).\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/applications, POST /admin/applications/new, POST /admin/applications/edit and POST /admin/applications/owners` on the admin console.",
