@endpoint("/admin-api/applications/add-certificate",
  "post",
  #{
    `operationId`:"addApplicationCertificate",
    `summary`:"Store a certificate on an application's entry, so an outside certificate authority's certificate authenticates it",
    `description`:"Stores one X.509 certificate in the application's `userCertificate` (RFC 4523; written as `userCertificate;binary`). A certificate from an outside certificate authority — one trusted through the Client Truststores — is an identity at a door that reads a client certificate as an application (a Shared Signals receiver's, for one) only while it is stored, byte for byte, on exactly one entry of the realm: never by its common name or subject (#1061, #1227). Refused when it is not one certificate (STS-ADMIN-0897), when it is already stored on another entry (STS-ADMIN-0899) or the registry holds no such application (STS-ADMIN-0906). A renewed certificate is stored again. Sends a CAEP credential-change (x509) under the application's own subject. RFC 8705's token endpoint does not read it: `tls_client_auth` keeps its own registered subject.\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/applications, POST /admin/applications/new, POST /admin/applications/edit and POST /admin/applications/owners` on the admin console.",
