@endpoint("/admin-api/applications/import-ldif",
  "post",
  #{
    `operationId`:"importApplicationLdif",
    `summary`:"Create an application from an LDIF file",
    `description`:"Reads an RFC 2849 LDIF document holding ONE application record, as `export-ldif` writes it, and creates that application in the realm this is called in, through every check a create makes. **IT NEVER OVERWRITES**: an identifier already recorded here is refused, naming it.\n\nOnly declared attributes are taken; a record carrying what this service records about use (a counter, a sighting, an observed value) is refused, naming each, and so is one carrying an attribute outside the schema or a credential no import can write. Credential material in the file is sealed on the way in exactly as a typed value is; client secrets keep their ids and expiries. Give the document as `ldif` (its text), or as `file` (its name and text), which is how the console sends an uploaded file.\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/applications, POST /admin/applications/new, POST /admin/applications/edit and POST /admin/applications/owners` on the admin console.",
