    `description`:"THE ONE OPERATION HERE THAT LOSES A FACT, which is why it is separate from `revoke-registration` rather than something that one does as well. The entry goes and takes its counters, its sightings and its attributes with it — for a client_id somebody typed wrong, or a realm from a test that is over.\n\nIt will reappear, EMPTY, the next time that identifier is accepted by a protocol: this registry records what this service has seen, and it is still seeing.\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/applications, POST /admin/applications/new, POST /admin/applications/edit and POST /admin/applications/owners` on the admin console.",
