@endpoint("/admin-api/xacml/disable-pep",
  "post",
  #{
    `operationId`:"disableXacmlPep",
    `summary`:"Stop nudging a registered remote PEP",
    `description`:"IT DOES NOT STOP IT ENFORCING, and the reply says so rather than letting that be discovered. A remote PEP holds its own copy of the engine and its own copy of the policy; nothing in this API reaches into another process. What changes is that this service no longer dials it when the repository changes, so it converges only on its own polling interval.\n\nNamed with a `-pep` suffix rather than reusing `disable` because this endpoint dispatches on the action name across the whole family, and a second `disable` would be ambiguous between a policy and a PEP.\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/xacml#xacml-tab-policies, POST /admin/xacml#xacml-tab-editor, POST /admin/xacml#xacml-tab-peps, POST /admin/xacml/policies, POST /admin/xacml/editor and POST /admin/xacml/peps` on the admin console.",
    `tags`:#["XACML"],
    `responses`:#{
      `200`:#{
        `description`:"The operation was applied.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `400`:#{
        `description`:"The operation was refused; `errors` says why and nothing changed.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `default`:#{
        `description`:"A refusal or a failure.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      }
    },
    `requestBody`:#{`required`:true,`content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}},
    `security`:#[#{`oauth2`:#["admin:write"]},#{`bearerAuth`:#[]}]
  })
op `disableXacmlPep`(@js(#{`examples`:#[#{`name`:"pep-1"}]}) `requestBody/content/application~1json/schema`: {@js(#{`description`:"The registered PEP's name."}) `name`: string},
