@endpoint("/admin-api/caep",
  "get",
  #{
    `operationId`:"getCaep",
    `summary`:"The CAEP session register: what state each session is in and how many events of which type have been sent about it",
    `description`:"Everything /admin/caep and /admin/caep-sessions draw, as JSON. Per session: who it belongs to, when it was established, the CAEP state it is in — established, presented, revoked — its assurance level, its device compliance, its risk level, the claims that have changed, and a count per event type.\n\nTHE REGISTER OUTLIVES THE SESSION AND THAT IS THE POINT. The session store forgets one the moment it is signed out, so a row saying `revoked` is the only remaining evidence that it existed and was revoked.\n\nCAEP IS A VOCABULARY AND NOT A FAMILY. Its events travel on SSF streams, are signed by the SSF signer and are delivered by the two SSF deliveries, so GET /admin-api/ssf is where the streams themselves are. `streams` here says only which of them would take a CAEP event at all, because a session with a count of zero almost always means nobody asked for that type — and SSF gives a receiver no other notice of that.\n\n**Mirrors** `GET /admin/caep` on the admin console.",
    `tags`:#["CAEP"],
    `responses`:#{
      `200`:#{
        `description`:"The register, the catalogue and the settings.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `default`:#{
        `description`:"A refusal or a failure.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      }
    },
    `security`:#[#{`oauth2`:#["admin:read"]},#{`bearerAuth`:#[]}]
  })
op `getCaep`(`responses/200/content/application~1json/schema`: `Caep`,
  `responses/default/content/application~1json/schema`: `SharedModel1`): void;
  

