@endpoint("/admin-api/scim",
  "get",
  #{
    `operationId`:"getScim",
    `summary`:"The SCIM 2.0 provisioning surface, and what it has been asked to do",
    `description`:"Counters and capabilities in one reply. The counters say which SCIM operation was performed how many times, on which resource type, and what was refused with which `scimType`; every operation and resource type is listed INCLUDING the ones at zero, because \"does this server do PATCH\" is otherwise answered by omission. The capabilities say what the endpoints are, what SCIM here deliberately does not do, and which LDAP attribute each SCIM member is.\n\nTHERE IS NO POST BESIDE THIS ONE and that is not a gap: everything about SCIM that can be changed is a configuration row — `scim.enabled`, the three limits and the authentication settings — so POST /admin-api/config/set is already the operation for it. The console page has no form on it either, which is the parity rule holding rather than being broken.\n\nWHAT SCIM WROTE is not here: it went into the embedded directory, so a person provisioned over SCIM is on /admin-api/users and their groups are on /admin-api/groups. There is no second store to report.\n\n**Mirrors** `GET /admin/scim` on the admin console.\n\nThe reply also carries `protocolEndpoints`: every endpoint of this family in the realm the call arrived in, as `{ name, methods, url }` (plus `route` for an HTTP endpoint, `transport` for a socket, and `registered: false` for a route the router no longer has).",
    `tags`:#["SCIM"],
    `responses`:#{
      `200`:#{
        `description`:"The counters and the capabilities.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `default`:#{
        `description`:"A refusal or a failure.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      }
    },
    `parameters`:#[
      #{
        `name`:"client",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"One outbound SCIM client's identifier (#552): `scimClients.client` is then that client's page — its queues, dead letters and discovery."
      }
    ],
    `security`:#[#{`oauth2`:#["admin:read"]},#{`bearerAuth`:#[]}]
  })
