@endpoint("/admin-api/kerberos/trusts/add",
  "post",
  #{
    `operationId`:"addKerberosTrust",
    `summary`:"Add a trust with another Kerberos realm",
    `description`:"Writes a trust record in this realm's directory (`ou=kerberosTrusts`) for `partnerRealm`. `direction` decides which keys it holds — `inbound` the incoming `krbtgt/<us>@<partner>` (the partner's tickets are accepted), `outbound` the outgoing `krbtgt/<partner>@<us>` (this realm refers to the partner), `bidirectional` both — and `keySource` where each comes from: `password`, a shared trust password both KDCs derive the key from (RFC 3961 string-to-key, RFC 4120's default salt), written and never shown back; or `generate`, random keys returned ONCE in `shown`. `attributes` are [MS-ADTS] 6.1.6.7.9's bits by name (`quarantined` by default); a contradiction or a missing requirement is refused. `forestTrustInfo` belongs to a cross-forest trust only. Refused for this realm's own name, a partner already held, and every field out of shape, each with its own code.\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/kerberos#kerberos-tab-trusts, POST /admin/kerberos/trusts` on the admin console.",
    `tags`:#["Kerberos"],
    `responses`:#{
      `200`:#{
        `description`:"The record's public view in `trust`, and a generated key once in `shown`.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `400`:#{
