    `description`:"New keys for `side` (`both`, the default, `incoming` or `outgoing`, of the sides held) at the current kvno plus one, from `keySource`. The incoming version it replaces still opens the partner's tickets for `krb5.trustKeyGraceSeconds` (by default the ticket lifetime plus the clock skew) and is refused KRB_AP_ERR_BADKEYVER after it. With `mirror: true` and a `trust-realm` partner, that realm's record is rotated in the same act the other way round — a service administrator's act. Without it the partner's administrator gives their side the same password or the keys in `shown`.\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/kerberos#kerberos-tab-trusts, POST /admin/kerberos/trusts` on the admin console.",
    `tags`:#["Kerberos"],
    `responses`:#{
      `200`:#{
        `description`:"The record's view, the sides rotated, the partner realm's record when mirrored, and a generated key once in `shown`.",
