@endpoint("/admin-api/roles",
  "get",
  #{
    `operationId`:"getRoles",
    `summary`:"Who holds a role, and what requires one",
    `description`:"The role register, both relations.\n\n**A role is a name somebody may hold, and holding one is what an ISSUANCE is decided on.** Three kinds of thing can be mapped into one — a person, a GROUP (so every member of it holds the role, resolved at decision time) and an APPLICATION, which is what a `client_credentials` grant is decided on where there is no person at all.\n\n**`roles` is MEMBERSHIP and `requiring` is REQUIREMENT, and they are opposite.** Membership is stored on the ROLE entry under `ou=roles` and is written through this resource. A requirement is `appRequiredRole` on an APPLICATION's own entry and is written through `POST /admin-api/applications/add` — one store, one door that writes it. It is READ here because this is the only surface that can resolve it: `requiring[].unknown` names a role an application demands that NOTHING defines, which refuses everybody, silently and correctly, and looks exactly like the application being broken.\n\n**Only NARROWED applications are in `requiring`.** An application that names no required role requires `EVERYBODY`, everybody holds `EVERYBODY`, and nothing is refused — which is how this service behaved before roles existed and is what makes the feature off by default without being absent.\n\n**The six `builtIn` roles are COMPUTED and in no container.** They cannot be created, edited or deleted, they have no members, and every one of them is answered from the CONTEXT of the decision being made. They are never in the roles claim either: `EVERYBODY` and `ALL_AUTHENTICATED_USERS` are true of almost every token this service issues, so carrying them would tell a relying party nothing it did not know from holding the token.\n\n`gated: false` means the XACML family is not loaded in this process, so `common/issuance_gate.js` has no decider and every issuance is allowed whatever this register says. `enforced: false` means `roles.enforceIssuance` is off, which is the same outcome by a different route and is the way back if a policy edit locks something out.\n\n**Mirrors** `GET /admin/roles` on the admin console.",
    `tags`:#["Roles"],
    `responses`:#{
      `200`:#{
        `description`:"The six built-in roles, every configured role with its three membership lists, every application that has been narrowed, and whether the decision is being asked for at all.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `400`:#{
        `description`:"The answer.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `default`:#{
        `description`:"A refusal or a failure.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      }
    },
    `parameters`:#[
      #{
        `name`:"q",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"Narrows the configured roles to those whose name, description or a member contains this."
      },
      #{
        `name`:"role",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"One role's name (#604): the answer also carries `role` — the role in full, its `owners` resolved, `requiredBy` (the applications whose requirement names it) and its directory `entry` — or `role.found: false`."
      },
      #{
        `name`:"rolesPage",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"Which page of the configured roles the search matched, answered by `paging` and `shownRoles`; twenty-five by default."
      },
      #{
        `name`:"per",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"Rows per page. Defaults to 50 and is capped at 300. On a drill-down it is SHARED by every list in the reply, which each carry a page number of their own."
      },
      #{
        `name`:"requiringPage",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"Which page of `requiring` to return, answered by `requiringPaging`. The applications that narrowed the roles they require (#313); `requiringPaging` says where the page is and `counts.requiring` counts them all."
      }
    ],
    `security`:#[#{`oauth2`:#["admin:read"]},#{`bearerAuth`:#[]}]
  })
