    `description`:"One role, group, service account or application (#607): `found`, its `dn`, its `owners` (DNs as stored), `protected` — whether it is CLOSED to its owners, who may then not administer it through this API with owner:read and owner:write — with `reasons`, one sentence each, and `marked`, whether an administrator's mark is one of them. An object is closed when it is a native or built-in role, a role authorizing a permission of this service, a group this service grants through by its name or a member of such a role, one of this service's own applications or one declaring or holding such a permission, a service account holding one, or marked.\n\n**Mirrors** `no console form — the owner rule's facts; the mark is stsOwnerProtected on the entry` on the admin console.",
