@endpoint("/admin-api/policies",
  "get",
  #{
    `operationId`:"getPolicies",
    `summary`:"The policies this realm holds a credential to",
    `description`:"Every kind of policy and its profiles — the PASSWORD POLICY and the AUTHENTICATION POLICY (#64), one profile each, `default`. Each kind is a member named by its id (`password`, `authn`) and a row of `kinds`.\n\n**`<kind>.profile` is the profile IN FORCE**: the stored entry where there is one (`stored: true`) and the built-in defaults where there is not — and, for the authentication policy only, the DEFAULT REALM's entry in a realm with none of its own (`from: \"default-realm\"`). `sources` says where each value came from, and `problems` names any stored value that could not be read.\n\n**`enforced` is whether this realm checks the password policy**, which is product mode. The authentication policy decides what the sign-in screen offers in both modes; `authn.mail.usable` says whether its two email mechanisms can be on here, and a field with `disabled: true` cannot be turned on until it can.\n\n**`attributes` is the attribute policy (#396)**: `required` the attributes every person here must hold, `catalogue` every attribute a person may be given (each `locked`, `required`, `custom`), `custom` the realm's own attributes, `enforced` whether it is enforced (product mode), and `missingFilter` the LDAP filter finding a person who lacks one.\n\n**`passkey.clients` is the realm's learned passkey clients (#1112)**: the browsers, systems and major versions a registration stopped offering ML-DSA to under `webauthn.clientLearning` (`learning` says whether it is on, `threshold` and `windowHours` its two settings), and those still being counted, each `client`, `learned`, `learnedAt`, `learnedFailures`, `failures` (in the window), `firstAt` and `lastAt`; learned first. Paged by `clientsPage` and `clientsPer` (`paging`), apart from the profiles. `clear-passkey-client` and `clear-passkey-clients` clear them.\n\n**A kind with NAMED profiles (#535, #1235)** carries `selectors` (the selector fields its save takes), `references` (the attribute by which an `application`, a `group` and/or a `person` names one of its profiles: `appPasskeyPolicy` and `stsPasskeyPolicy` for the passkey policy; `stsServiceAccountPolicy`, on a service account and nobody else, for the service-account policy (#1240)) and `named`, each profile with its `precedence` and `namedBy` — the `applications`, `groups` and `people` whose reference names it. Of the profile an application names, the profile a person names and the profiles the person's groups name, the lowest `precedence` applies (ties by name), else `default`; a profile something still names cannot be deleted.\n\nIt is NOT the XACML policy repository, which is `GET /admin-api/xacml/policies`.\n\n**Mirrors** `GET /admin/policies` on the admin console.",
    `tags`:#["Policies"],
    `responses`:#{
      `200`:#{
        `description`:"The kinds of policy, each kind's profile in force with its field table and schema, and the paged profiles.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `400`:#{
        `description`:"The answer.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `default`:#{
        `description`:"A refusal or a failure.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      }
    },
    `parameters`:#[
      #{
        `name`:"page",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"Which page of the match to return. CLAMPED rather than refused: a page past the end returns the last one, and the reply says which page it actually is."
      },
      #{
        `name`:"per",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"Rows per page. Defaults to 50 and is capped at 300. On a drill-down it is SHARED by every list in the reply, which each carry a page number of their own."
      },
      #{
        `name`:"missing",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"`count` answers `attributes.missing`: how many people in this realm lack a value of an attribute the attribute policy requires. A walk of the realm's people, so asked only on request, and null where the directory is held in the store (`attributes.missingFilter` is the LDAP filter that finds them there)."
      },
      #{
        `name`:"clientsPage",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"Which page of `passkey.clients.rows`, the learned passkey clients. Defaults to 1."
      },
      #{
        `name`:"clientsPer",
        `in`:"query",
        `required`:false,
        `schema`:null,
        `description`:"Rows per page of `passkey.clients.rows`. Defaults to 25."
      }
    ],
    `security`:#[#{`oauth2`:#["admin:read"]},#{`bearerAuth`:#[]}]
  })
op `getPolicies`(@js(#{`minimum`:1}) `parameters/0/schema`: integer,
