@endpoint("/admin-api/policies/save-serviceAccount-policy",
  "post",
  #{
    `operationId`:"saveServiceAccountPolicy",
    `summary`:"Set the service-account policy profile",
    `description`:"Writes `cn=default,ou=serviceAccountPolicies` in this realm's directory, REPLACING what is there; a realm with no entry of its own follows the default realm's. Every default is the more secure one: no second-factor exemption, no browser sign-in, no rotation, an owner required. Two rules read other registers: `generatedLength` may not be below the password policy's `minLength`, and `rotationEnabled` is refused while the realm has no push destination. The seven `allow*` door fields say which password doors a service account may use. **A NAMED profile (#1240)** — `profile` of lower-case letters, digits and hyphens, with `precedence` — is this realm's own and governs every service account whose `stsServiceAccountPolicy` names it (set on the person's Policies tab or by `POST /admin-api/users/set-attribute`; only a service account may hold it, STS-SVCACCT-0048). A reference the realm does not hold gets `default` and is logged (STS-SVCACCT-0047), and a named profile an account still names is not deleted (STS-SVCACCT-0049).\n\n**Every field is required** and one left out is refused by name rather than reset to a default, because a save that quietly loosened a rule nobody mentioned is the mistake nobody sees.\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/policies` on the admin console.",
    `tags`:#["Policies"],
    `responses`:#{
      `200`:#{
        `description`:"The profile now in force and the rules as sentences.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
