  #{
    `operationId`:"createSpiffeJoinToken",
    `summary`:"Mint a join token for a workload agent",
    `description`:"How an operator provisions the sidecar agent that serves the Workload API on a Unix socket next to a workload (#324). The SPIRE Server API is what the agent attests to; this is the same join-token store `CreateJoinToken` writes, reached here because there is no admin SVID until a Workload API exists to fetch one from.\n\nThe token is shown once, in `token` and in `message`, and is not recorded. `agentSpiffeId` is the identity the token will attest, which is a digest of the token and is safe to keep: parent that agent's workload entries on it. An optional `agentId` registers an alias the way SPIRE does, and is not the `agent` field the ban takes.\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/spiffe/agents` on the admin console.",
