  #{
    `operationId`:"deletePushedRequest",
    `summary`:"Withdraw a pushed authorization request (RFC 9126)",
    `description`:"Removes one pushed request, named by the SHA-256 of its request_uri, from this realm's store of pushed authorization requests, live or spent. The authorization endpoint refuses it from then on with 400 invalid_request_uri, exactly as it refuses one that expired and was swept; a browser already on the sign-in or consent screen with it is refused when it comes back. Counted as `par.deleted` and written to the audit log. A value that is not a handle (43 characters of base64url), or one this realm does not hold, is refused 400. The store keeps no request_uri (#614), so the handle is the only name it answers to.\n\n**Mirrors** `POST /admin/oauth2/monitor` on the admin console.",
