@endpoint("/admin-api/passkey-report",
  "get",
  #{
    `operationId`:"getPasskeyReport",
    `summary`:"Who holds which passkey algorithm, across the realm (#942)",
    `description`:"Everything Monitoring → Passkeys draws. `people`: `total`, `holding`, `postQuantumOnly`, `classicalOnly`, `both`, `none` and `withPostQuantum` — a person's kind is the ALGORITHM of their keys (ML-DSA is post-quantum), never the lane. `keys`: `total`, `postQuantum`, `classical`, `byLane` and `byAlgorithm` (each `algorithm`, `coseAlg`, `lane`, `postQuantum`, `count`). `models`: each AAGUID with its name and the algorithms its keys use. `attestation`: the leaf certificate's signature algorithm (#941). `recorded` is false when no counted passkey stored one. `profiles`: each passkey profile's `postQuantumRequired` and selectors. `counted`: where the numbers came from — the recount's `baseline` (when, how long, how many holders) plus the `changesSince` noted as keys were written, or the `population` a filter read; null before the first recount. With `list`, a page of the people behind one count, paged by `page`, `per` and `from` (the cursor `list.paging.nextFrom` hands back); a realm list reads at most 20000 entries a request and says `complete: false` when that stopped it. NO COUNT IS A SCAN OF THE DIRECTORY: the realm's are a maintained aggregate.\n\n**Mirrors** `GET /admin/passkey-report` on the admin console.",
    `tags`:#["Monitoring"],
    `responses`:#{
      `200`:#{
        `description`:"The report.",
        `content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}
      },
      `400`:#{
